Package: bee-pagoda
Version: 0.1.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: bash (>= 5.0), python3 (>= 3.10)
Recommends: sysbench, fio, ffmpeg, p7zip-full, python3-pip
Suggests: nvidia-utils-525, clinfo, opencl-headers
Maintainer: Bee Pagoda Benchmark Contributors <bee-pagoda@example.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/bhocking2009-lang/bee-pagoda-benchmark
Description: Automated Linux system benchmark suite
 Bee Pagoda Benchmark is a comprehensive, automated Linux host benchmark
 suite for measuring CPU throughput, GPU compute, AI inference, memory
 bandwidth, and storage performance.
 .
 Features:
  - CPU: sysbench baseline, 7z compression, ffmpeg encode (with pre-probe)
  - GPU compute: clpeak / hashcat fallback; vendor auto-detection
  - GPU graphics: glmark2 / vkmark; session-aware offscreen/interactive
  - AI: llama.cpp, ONNX Runtime, PyTorch (multi-backend composite score)
  - Memory: sysbench memory + tinymembench
  - Storage: fio sequential + random 4K (safe file-based)
  - Stress: mixed CPU+memory load, throttling detection, thermal trend
 .
 Each run produces structured JSON/CSV/Markdown reports with normalized
 metrics, health bands, compare-to-previous delta, and SQLite trend history.
